  '{"id":"KAEU4MMrCCo","title":"ISTANBUL TURKEY 2026 4K WALKING TOUR | Sultanahmet to Eminönü, Markets, Street Food & Taksim","description":"Experience Istanbul in one complete 2 hours 40 minutes 4K walking tour, covering some of the city’s most famous historic streets, waterfront areas, markets, food spots, and modern tourist districts. This full city walk takes you through the heart of Istanbul, from the Old City atmosphere around Sultanahmet to Sirkeci, Eminönü, and the lively streets around Taksim.\n\nThe journey begins in Istanbul’s historic center, where centuries-old architecture, mosques, public squares, traditional shops, and busy pedestrian streets create the classic Old City atmosphere. Along the route, you will see areas near Sultanahmet Square, Hagia Sophia, the Blue Mosque, Gülhane, Sirkeci, and the roads leading toward Eminönü and the Golden Horn.\n\nThis video is ideal for viewers searching for an Istanbul Turkey 2026 walking tour, a full Istanbul city walk, Sultanahmet to Eminönü routes, Istanbul markets, street food, crowds, shopping streets, and real daily life. The extended length allows you to experience different parts of the city naturally, from historical neighborhoods and waterfront traffic to modern streets filled with tourists, cafés, shops, and local activity.\n\nAround Sirkeci and Eminönü, discover busy market streets, Turkish flags, local vendors, souvenir shops, spice displays, sweets, street-food stalls, ferries, and views across the water. Look out for popular foods such as simit, döner, balık ekmek, grilled corn, roasted chestnuts, baklava, Turkish delight, fresh juice, tea, and Turkish coffee. The area is also a good place to browse spices, accessories, ceramics, textiles, souvenirs, and traditional gifts.\n\nThe tour also includes the wider Taksim and Beyoğlu atmosphere, where Istanbul’s historic character meets modern city life. These areas are known for crowded pedestrian streets, international visitors, cafés, restaurants, shopping, street fashion, and easy connections to Galata, Karaköy, Istiklal Street, and the Bosphorus.\n\nVisitors can reach these areas using Istanbul’s tram, metro, ferry, Marmaray, buses, and walking connections. Sultanahmet and Sirkeci are served by the T1 tram, Eminönü has major ferry and tram links, and Taksim is connected by the M2 metro, buses, and the historic funicular routes. Enjoy this long Istanbul Turkey 2026 4K walking tour and explore the Old City, markets, street food, waterfront life, crowds, and Taksim in one complete journey.\n\n#Istanbul #IstanbulTurkey #Istanbul2026 #IstanbulWalkingTour #4KWalkingTour #Sultanahmet #Eminonu #Sirkeci #Taksim #IstanbulOldCity #IstanbulMarkets #IstanbulStreetFood #TurkeyTravel #IstanbulTour #MyDeliciousTrips\n\n\nISTANBUL TURKEY 2026 4K WALKING TOUR | Old City, Markets, Street Food, Eminönü & Taksim\nISTANBUL TURKEY 2026 4K WALKING TOUR | Sultanahmet to Eminönü, Markets, Street Food & Taksim\nISTANBUL TURKEY 2026 4K WALKING TOUR | Full City Walk, Old City Markets, Street Food & Taksim\n\n00:00 my delicious trips\n00:06 video highlights\n03:11 around sultanahmet\n05:00 Tarihi Sultanahmet Köftecisi Selim Usta\n09:30 istanbul hop on hop off bus\n12:40 German Fountain\n17:00 Obelisk of Theodosius\n22:00 The Blue Mosque\n37:00 sultanahmet area\n43:43 viyana kahvesi sultanahmet\n45:00 sultanahmet restaurants\n56:45 yerebatan street sultanahmet\n1:06:30 gulhane park\n1:13:00 around sirkeci\n1:21:20 sirkeci restaurants\n1:26:30 tatlici safa sirkeci\n1:38:43 spice bazaar eminonu\n1:44:30 eminonu market\n1:52:00 eminonu square\n1:59:30 galata bridge\n2:01:00 istiklal street\n\nBehind every video there are hours of walking, filming, batteries, memory cards, and late-night edits. If my content adds value to your day, consider tipping a coffee: Buy Me a Coffee\n ☕️\nYour support directly funds new routes, better audio, and upgraded lenses. Thank you for helping this channel grow! 🌍🎥\n\nhttp://bit.ly/3WO8jle\n\n🚷If you appear in thi