  '{"id":"FlFDB1rMOX8","title":"ISTANBUL, Türkiye 🇹🇷 The Most Magical City on Earth? 4K Walking Tour","description":"This 4K Istanbul walking tour takes you from Sultanahmet Square with the Blue Mosque and Hagia Sophia through the old city streets to the Grand Bazaar, Spice Bazaar, Eminönü, and across the Galata Bridge into Karaköy. It’s a full Istanbul city walk in 4K UHD, filmed in real-time with no music and no commentary – the best way to experience the real atmosphere of Istanbul.\n\nWe begin in the heart of Sultanahmet, exploring landmarks like the Blue Mosque, Hagia Sophia (Ayasofya-i Kebir Mosque), and Sultanahmet Park. The walk continues along Divan Yolu and Bab-ı Ali Street into the bustling markets of Nuru Osmaniye Street and the Grand Bazaar (Kapalı Çarşı). From there, we pass through Beyazıt to the Spice Bazaar (Mısır Çarşısı), before reaching Eminönü with its historic Yeni Camii and lively square. The tour ends with views of the Golden Horn, a walk over the Galata Bridge, and into the streets of Karaköy.\n\n🎥 Perfect for those searching for Istanbul walking tour 4K, Istanbul old city walk, Hagia Sophia walking tour, Istanbul bazaar walk, Galata Bridge 4K, or virtual tours of Istanbul Türkiye.\n\n📍 Tour Highlights:\n🕌 Blue Mosque & Sultanahmet Square – Ottoman masterpiece\n⛲ German Fountain & Sultanahmet Park – Historic city center\n🕌 Hagia Sophia (Ayasofya-i Kebir Mosque) – Icon of Istanbul\n🚶 Divan Yolu & Bab-ı Ali Street – Main streets of the old city\n🛍️ Nuruosmaniye Mosque & Street – Gateway to the bazaars\n🛒 Grand Bazaar – Kapalı Çarşı, one of the world’s largest covered markets\n🌶️ Egyptian Bazaar (Spice Bazaar) – Colors, aromas & sounds of Istanbul\n⛪ Yeni Camii – The New Mosque at Eminönü\n🌉 Galata Bridge – Fishing, views & crossing the Golden Horn\n🎨 Karaköy – Trendy district with cafés and street life\n\n📌 About Istanbul, Türkiye:\nIstanbul is Türkiye’s largest city and a cultural capital that blends Byzantine, Ottoman, and modern influences. From the mosques of Sultanahmet to the historic bazaars and the lively waterfront of Eminönü and Karaköy, the city shows why it’s one of the most visited destinations in the world. This Istanbul walking tour in 4K captures history, daily life, and the unique atmosphere of a city between Europe and Asia.\n\n🕒 Chapters:\n00:00 Blue Mosque & Obelisk of Theodosius\n02:45 German Fountain\n04:23 Sultanahmet Park\n06:41 Hagia Sophia – Ayasofya-i Kebir Mosque\n11:22 Divan Yolu Street\n17:00 Bab-ı Ali Street\n19:50 Nuru Osmaniye Street\n23:00 Nuruosmaniye Mosque\n27:44 Grand Bazaar – Kapalı Çarşı\n32:12 Streets of Beyazıt\n43:40 Egyptian Bazaar – Spice Bazaar – Mısır Çarşısı\n48:40 Eminönü Yeni Camii\n52:42 Eminönü Square\n55:09 Eminönü Tunnel Shopping\n57:03 Famous Place at Eminönü\n58:07 Golden Horn – Haliç View\n1:02:12 View Point\n1:04:18 Galata Bridge\n1:12:34 Karaköy\n\n🎬 Filming Info:\n📍 Location: Istanbul, Türkiye\n📽️ Format: 4K UHD at 60fps\n🎧 Audio: Real city sounds – no music, no commentary\n☀️ Time: Daytime, September 2025\n\nWhich part of this Istanbul walking tour would you enjoy most – exploring Hagia Sophia and the Blue Mosque, shopping at the Grand Bazaar and Spice Bazaar, or walking across the Galata Bridge into Karaköy?\n\n🤝 Business Inquiries and Contact: walkingozmedia@gmail.com\n\n⚠️ My videos are copyrighted material owned by the channel Walking OZ. Any unauthorized use, including for personal or private purposes, is strictly prohibited. Walking OZ reserves the right to issue copyright strikes for infringement, and will not withdraw them once issued.","thumbnail":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/FlFDB1rMOX8/hqdefault.jpg","category":"Walking Tours","channel":"Walking OZ","channelTitle":"Walking OZ","channelId":"UC20vyRWEaC2GIS8DkmeRQaA","badge":"4K 60FPS","publishedAt":"2025-09-20T12:04:10Z","city":"Istanbul","country":"Türkiye","duration":"PT1H35M52S","active":true,"embedAvailable":true,"thumbnailValid":true,"chapters":[{"title":"Blue Mosque & Obelisk of Theodosius","startSeconds":0,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":165},{"title":"German Fountain","startSeconds":165,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":263},{"title":"Sultanahmet Park","startSeconds":263,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":401},{"title":"Hagia Sophia – Ayasofya-i Kebir Mosque","startSeconds":401,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":682},{"title":"Divan Yolu Street","startSeconds":682,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":1020},{"title":"Bab-ı Ali Street","startSeconds":1020,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":1190},{"title":"Nuru Osmaniye Street","startSeconds":1190,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":1380},{"title":"Nuruosmaniye Mosque","startSeconds":1380,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":1664},{"title":"Grand Bazaar – Kapalı Çarşı","startSeconds":1664,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":1932},{"title":"Streets of Beyazıt","startSeconds":1932,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":2620},{"title":"Egyptian Bazaar – Spice Bazaar – Mısır Çarşısı","startSeconds":2620,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":2920},{"title":"Eminönü Yeni Camii","startSeconds":2920,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":3162},{"title":"Eminönü Square","startSeconds":3162,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":3309},{"title":"Eminönü Tunnel Shopping","startSeconds":3309,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":3423},{"title":"Famous Place at Eminönü","startSeconds":3423,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":3487},{"title":"