SOHO is a neighborhood in Lower Manhattan in New York City. Since the 20th century it has been the location of many artists'' lofts and art galleries, and has also been known for its variety of shops ranging from trendy upscale boutiques to national and international chain store outlets. The area''s history is an archetypal example of inner-city regeneration and gentrification, encompassing socioeconomic, cultural, political, and architectural developments.
