  '{"id":"uOJkVLwnCNI","title":"Rome, Italy Walking Tour - 4K60fps with Captions - Prowalk Tours","description":"This walking tour of Rome, Italy was filmed on Saturday May 14th starting at 11:10 AM at the Spanish Steps.\n\n🗺️Map of the Walk - https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=1zzTsqE1ZSlkRA2KBlw5AXWGo9kHsJr0&usp=sharing 🗺️\n\n🔻Video Timeline Links🔻\n0:00 Intro and Map\n1:25 Spanish Steps\n32:11 Trevi Fountain\n49:39 Piazza di Pietra\n55:18 Pantheon\n1:11:00 Church of St. Louis of the French\n1:19:51 Piazza Navona\n1:32:29 Statua di Pasquino\n1:39:36 Campo de''Fiori\n1:59:06 Portico of Ocatvia\n2:03:48 Teatro Marcello\n2:10:43 Capitoline Hill\n2:35:20 Altar of the Fatherland\n3:01:29 Trajan''s Forum\n3:12:55 Forum of Augustus\n3:25:33 Basilica dei Santi Cosma e Damiano\n3:37:38 Colosseum\n\n▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬\n📽 *MORE WALKING TOURS*\n▪Christmas Markets Playlist: (https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLSOO4vYXpMCd2nqHyPaDtgxkf_BsAuQCt&si=0YU1zhv0tLbwm8u6)\n▪ Italy Playlist: (https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLSOO4vYXpMCc6k7EuMhr764qCNeXDrxpj&si=aYfLAtNw1eGc560w)\n▪ Greece Playlist: (https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLSOO4vYXpMCf151n5M3j9IxxvvvZNK7TM&si=xW-ewBTs4pzb90a1)\n▪ Biking Tours Playlist: (https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLSOO4vYXpMCe4SaQXMk9IMfpkl1w473Zz&si=1rFBHTnZtCMmykPA)\n▪ Egypt Playlist: (https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLSOO4vYXpMCc_y7TUiJufW_N_QZod0M8d&si=XgIlOOZb0DLiPt9z)\n▪ Japan Playlist: (https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLSOO4vYXpMCc69vi-SFMODDGKQf_7D-IK&si=hxZIpoG9x1Ypszyq)\n▪ Brazil Playlist: (https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLSOO4vYXpMCcefbIXpStQK7fPRJBBiBAH&si=Zlji0Mfbp3sJlyjs)\n▪ Australia Playlist: (https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLSOO4vYXpMCcuh1sGTbEtCldxhCA6grbV&si=tQ56vSTmsQKUNWjN)\n▪ Complete List of Walks: http://www.prowalks.com/videos\n▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬\n\n===============================================================================\n📢 *SUPPORT & CONNECT* 📢\n🌍 Website: https://www.prowalktours.com\n📧 Email: prowalktours@gmail.com\n🔔 Subscribe for more! (https://www.youtube.com/@ProwalkTours)\n🟥 Become a Member: (https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCNzul4dnciIlDg8BAcn5-cQ/join)\n🔶 Support me on Patreon - https://www.patreon.com/Prowalktours\n🔷 Help with a donation! - https://www.paypal.me/Prowalks\n👕Merchandise - https://teespring.com/stores/prowalk-tours\n===============================================================================\n\n▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬\n🎥 *MY FILMING GEAR (SHOP LINKS BELOW!)* 🎥\n🌍 Amazon Storefront: https://www.amazon.com/shop/prowalktours\n🎥Camera: Sony a7siii: https://amzn.to/4hTUSJj\n📸Camera Lens: https://amzn.to/3UtuZUm\n🎬Gimbal: https://amzn.to/3FsDye5\n🎤Microphone: https://amzn.to/3lYW5CI\n🎧In-Ear Monitors: https://amzn.to/2DBdS1D\n▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬\n\n🚷 No portion of this video may be used without prior written consent from Prowalk Tours. If you appear in this video and wish to have your image removed, please contact me.\n\nInformation: Experience the timeless beauty of Rome in this extensive walking tour, taking you through the Eternal City''s most iconic landmarks. From the historic Spanish Steps to the grand Colosseum, this tour covers nearly four hours of Rome’s architectural wonders, charming piazzas, and ancient ruins. Whether you''re revisiting your favorite Roman spots or discovering them for the first time, this walking tour offers an in-depth journey through one of the most remarkable cities in the world.\n\nHistory: Rome’s history spans over 2,500 years, and this tour offers a glimpse into some of its most significant monuments. Starting at the Spanish Steps (1:25), which were built in the early 18th century and remain one of Rome’s most popular meeting spots, you’ll pass through the Trevi Fountain (32:11), an 18th-century Baroque masterpiece where visitors toss coins to ensure their return to Rome. At the Pantheon (55:18), you''ll explore the best-preserved Roman temple, dating back to 125 AD, and learn about its transformation into a Christian church. The tour also takes you to the Altar of the Fatherland (2:35:20), a monumental tribute to Italy''s first king, Victor Emmanuel II, and finishes with a close-up view of the Colosseum (3:37:38), the largest amphitheater ever built, which once hosted gladiatorial battles.\n\nTourist Tips:\n\nBegin your tour at the Spanish Steps (1:25) to enjoy the early morning light before the crowds gather.\nToss a coin into the Trevi Fountain (32:11) to ensure a future trip to Rome—just be sure to do it with your right hand over your left shoulder!\nTake a moment to admire the artistry at the Church of St. Louis of the French (1:11:00), which houses famous paintings by Caravaggio.\nEnjoy the vibrant atmosphere of Piazza Navona (1:19:51), surrounded by Baroque architecture and street performers.\nClimb up Capitoline Hill (2:10:43) for incredible views of the Roman Forum and cityscape.\nEnd your tour at the Colosseum (3:37:38), where you can imagine the grand gladiatorial contests that once took place within its walls.\n\n#ProwalkTours #Walkingtour #Rome","thumbnail":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uOJkVLwnCNI/hqdefault.jpg","category":"Walking Tours","channel":"Prowalk Tours","channelTitle":"Prowalk Tours","channelId":"UCNzul4dnciIlDg8BAcn5-cQ","badge":"4K 60FPS","publishedAt":"2023-05-20T13:00:01Z","city":"Rome","country":"Italy","duration":"PT3H50M43S","active":true,"embedAvailable":true,"thumbnailValid":true,"chapters":[{"title":"Spanish Steps","startSeconds":85,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":1931},{"title":"Trevi Fountain","startSeconds":1931,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":2979},{"title":"Piazza di Pietra","startSeconds":2979,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":3318},{"title":"Pantheon","startSeconds":3318,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":4260},{"title":"Church of St. Louis of the French","startSeconds