  '{"id":"SKJG4xqdH_0","title":"Spring Morning Walk through Historic Higashiyama | Kyoto, Japan 4K","description":"A quiet spring morning walking along Shirakawa River and Canal with sakura cherry blossoms in early bloom. I had intended to focus on the riverside as I thought cherry trees and traditional Japanese buildings would combine nicely with the gently flowing water sounds...but I figured since Gion was right there it might be nice to take a look in the early morning while the streets were quiet and empty. From there it seemed a shame not to walk through Yasaka Shrine and see it''s famous weeping cherry tree in bloom. There were a number of stalls sitting idly by waiting for the hanami crowds that I''m sure would soon arrive. There were a number of crows waiting as well.\n\nFrom there I climbed the steps to Chionin Temple, just as the monks began to chant their morning prayer. Eventually I made it back to Shirakawa River, and walked along at water''s edge through a quiet neighborhood, past the large torii gate in front of Heian Shrine, up Keage Slope (an old boat ramp connecting the Kyoto - Lake Biwa Canal), and finally along the aqueduct to Nanzenji. When I was thinking about the route, I thought it would take a little over an hour of walking, but with the diversions it ended up being closer to two. I hope you enjoy this extended walk through some beautiful areas of Kyoto just as spring begins.\n\nI hope the seasons are treating you well. I''ve linked the walk below if you''re interested .\n\nRoute Map:\nhttps://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=1FIsvFIPun9WWT9ADBheRIfuK9Bewglo&usp=sharing\n\nMarch 31, 2025\n\n*Subscribe* for more dawn walks in Japan and elsewhere: https://bit.ly/3IO4oxS\n\n**Playlists**\n\n**Dawn Walks** https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLvh9Rliu52xop6xDpoETQ3Yos-hYNfkU5\n\n**Japan Less Traveled**: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLvh9Rliu52xq1HdvglrnJxz7vwdqBxHV5\n\n**Japan Well Traveled:** https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLvh9Rliu52xpfk_D6oRuo_m86OOVjSnjP\n\n**Relaxing Environments:** https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLvh9Rliu52xq8PitzXKxwhvYA-uc_kP1N\n\n**Rain, Snow, and Weather:** https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLvh9Rliu52xrwO_Iy7r6r4D0ghHM7pYb4\n\n**Cities at Night:** https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLvh9Rliu52xph6UUdZhlBX0MHQtgaRkou\n\n00:00 Intro\n00:30 Shirakawa River\n09:49 Sakura street\n18:10 Tatsumi Bridge\n22:58 Shirakawa Canal\n30:36 Gion\n40:57 Yasaka Shrine\n48:04 Gion Weeping Cherry Tree\n52:04 Chionin Temple\n01:08:13 Chionin Kuromon\n01:15:12 River Terrace\n01:25:31 Heian-Jingu Shrine Grand Torii\n01:35:02 Keage Incline\n01:42:25 Keage Boat Reservoir\n01:52:50 Nanzen-ji Suirokaku\n\n#sakura #cherryblossoms #kyototravel #spring","thumbnail":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SKJG4xqdH_0/hqdefault.jpg","category":"Museums & Culture","channel":"Ambient Exploration","channelTitle":"Ambient Exploration","channelId":"UCTwtAPLzYSrqNCtmMw0YrRQ","badge":"4K 60FPS","publishedAt":"2025-04-01T11:49:00Z","city":"Kyoto","country":"Japan","duration":"PT2H6M52S","active":true,"embedAvailable":true,"thumbnailValid":true,"chapters":[{"title":"Shirakawa River","startSeconds":30,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":589},{"title":"Sakura street","startSeconds":589,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":1090},{"title":"Tatsumi Bridge","startSeconds":1090,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":1378},{"title":"Shirakawa Canal","startSeconds":1378,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":1836},{"title":"Gion","startSeconds":1836,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":2457},{"title":"Yasaka Shrine","startSeconds":2457,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":1,"endSeconds":2884},{"title":"Gion Weeping Cherry Tree","startSeconds":2884,"verified":true,"source":"youtube-description","confidence":