  '{"id":"a8ZCzEF2tfo","title":"CHAMPS-ÉLYSÉES, Paris 🇫🇷 The Most Beautiful Avenue in the World | Walking Tour | 4K 60FPS","description":"CHAMPS-ÉLYSÉES, Paris 🇫🇷 Walking down the most beautiful avenue in the world, from the Arc de Triomphe all the way to the Place de la Concorde, through the heart of Paris and its golden triangle of luxury. Filmed in stunning 4K Ultra HD 60FPS.\n\nToday I''m taking you with me on a walk through one of my favourite parts of Paris, the elegant 8th arrondissement. We start at the Arc de Triomphe, head down the legendary Champs-Élysées, and wander through the golden triangle of haute couture along Avenue Montaigne and Avenue George V, passing some of the most famous fashion houses, hotels and monuments in the world. We then make our way past the Élysée Palace and the Faubourg Saint-Honoré, before finishing at the magnificent Place de la Concorde. I''ve added captions along the way to share the history and little details behind everything we pass, so you feel like you''re really walking beside me.\n\n💡 Don''t forget to activate subtitles to discover all the secrets and stories behind everything you see in this video.\n\n🗺️ Here is the full route of this walk : https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=165d1oPKb4xYz8Gf7Wp8M9xRq4mhXnDY&usp=sharing\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n📅 Filmed on: Tuesday, June 17, 2026\n🕰 Start time: 12:43 PM\n🌞 Weather: 30°C | 86°F\n📍 Starting point: Métro Charles de Gaulle Étoile, Paris 8th, France\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n⏱️ TOUR TIMELINE\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n00:00 Intro\n00:36 Arc de Triomphe\n02:40 Champs-Élysées\n23:25 Avenue George V\n25:40 Rue François 1er\n29:24 Rue Marbeuf\n32:50 Avenue George V\n36:10 Avenue Montaigne\n49:44 Avenue Matignon\n57:03 Élysée Palace\n59:03 Rue du Faubourg Saint-Honoré\n1:06:44 Rue Royale & La Madeleine\n1:10:08 Place de la Concorde\n1:13:54 Outro\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n🇫🇷 ABOUT THE CHAMPS-ÉLYSÉES\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🌳 The Champs-Élysées stretches nearly 2 kilometers, from the Arc de Triomphe to the Place de la Concorde.\n👑 Its name means \"Elysian Fields\", a reference to the paradise of Greek mythology.\n🏛️ Often called \"La Plus Belle Avenue du Monde\", the most beautiful avenue in the world.\n🛍️ Home to flagship stores like Louis Vuitton, Cartier, Dior, and many more.\n🍽️ Famous addresses include Le Fouquet''s, Ladurée, and the legendary Plaza Athénée.\n🎖️ The Arc de Triomphe stands 50 meters tall, commissioned by Napoleon in 1806.\n💎 The golden triangle, between Avenue Montaigne, Avenue George V and the Champs-Élysées, is the epicentre of Parisian haute couture.\n🏛️ The Place de la Concorde is the largest square in Paris, home to the 3,300-year-old Luxor Obelisk.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n▶ WATCH NEXT\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nOn this channel, alongside my walking tours, I also take you inside the most iconic monuments. Here''s the full tour of the Eiffel Tower, from the ground all the way up to the summit.🗼\n\nhttps://youtu.be/LYPGVQWI7No\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nIf you enjoy these walks, consider subscribing to follow the next ones. I''ve got a lot more of Paris, and the world, still to explore with you.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n#paris #champselysees #walkingtour #4k #travel #france #europe #tourism #wanderlust #awalktour","thumbnail":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/a8ZCzEF2tfo/maxresdefault.jpg","category":"Walking Tours","channel":"a.walktour","channelTitle":"a.walktour","channelId":"UCQ8ZZiluVgKO_QpEZsIKvHw","badge":"4K 60FPS","publishedAt":"2026-06-20T12:00:27Z","admission":{"version":1,"status":"accepted","uniqueEvidenceCount":11,"evidence":[{"title":"Arc de Triomphe","startSeconds":36},{"title":"Champs-Élysées","startSeconds":160},{"title":"Avenue George V","startSeconds":1405},{"title":"Rue François 1er","startSeconds":1540},{"title":"Rue Marbeuf","startSeconds":1764},{"title":"Avenue Montaigne","startSeconds":2170}