Switzerland (or die Schweiz in German, La Suisse in French) is an country in Central Europe. Switzerland is officially known as Confederatio Helvetica. It borders Germany, Italy, France, Liechtenstein and Austria and is located high in the mountains of the Alps. The capital of Switzerland is Bern, but Zürich is the largest city and Geneva is the second most populous city. Switzerland has 4 official languages: German, French, Italian and a local language called Romansh. Switzerland has a population of 9 million.

