  '{"id":"BbCOFlpC-MQ","title":"4K Japan Walking Tour: Cherry blossom season in Tokyo","description":"This 210-minute Tokyo cherry blossom walking tour covers the world-famous Sakura Tunnel at Nihonbashi and the prestigious streets of Ginza during peak cherry blossom season. Walk from historic Kanda through over 150 cherry trees on Edo Sakura Street, explore ancient shrines, and experience the blend of traditional Tokyo and modern luxury during spring''s most vibrant season.\nCHERRY BLOSSOM SEASON IN TOKYO\nThis walking tour captures Tokyo''s cherry blossoms at their absolute peak—a brief seasonal window when the city transforms. The tour combines natural beauty (cherry trees, blooming flowers) with urban architecture and historic spiritual sites.\nNIHONBASHI SAKURA TUNNEL: EDO SAKURA STREET\nThe Sakura Tunnel features over 150 cherry trees lining Edo Sakura Street at Nihonbashi—one of Tokyo''s most stunning seasonal displays. Walking beneath the canopy shows the scale and beauty of this concentrated cherry blossom area.\nThe tunnel demonstrates how Tokyo creates seasonal focal points by concentrating natural elements in urban spaces.\nKANDA: HISTORIC TOKYO BACKSTREETS\nThe walk begins in Kanda''s nostalgic backstreets—areas preserving traditional Tokyo character. Walking through shows historic architecture, narrow lanes, and the older layers of Tokyo existing beneath modern development.\nGINZA: LUXURY AND ARCHITECTURE\nThe route continues to Ginza, Tokyo''s most famous district. Walking through Ginza during cherry blossom season shows the contrast between high-end retail, modern architecture, and delicate spring blooms.\nHISTORIC SHRINES AND SPIRITUAL SITES\nThe walk includes several ancient shrines:\n\nShirohata Inari Shrine\nFukutoku Shrine (ancient sanctuary)\nKarasumori Shrine (final destination)\n\nThese shrines show how Tokyo maintains spiritual sites throughout the commercial district.\nLANDMARKS AND ARCHITECTURE\nThe tour covers:\n\nNihonbashi Bridge (historic landmark)\nCoredo Muromachi (modern commercial complex)\nGinza Lion (architectural landmark)\nShimbashi transit hub\nVarious historic and modern buildings\n\nSEASONAL EXPERIENCE: CHERRY BLOSSOM SEASON\nThis 210-minute tour captures a specific moment—peak cherry blossom season—when Tokyo''s appearance changes dramatically. The cherry blossoms create atmosphere, attract crowds, and transform how neighborhoods feel.\nUnderstanding Tokyo during cherry blossom season means understanding how seasonality shapes urban experience and tourism in Japan.\n🕒 TIMESTAMPS\n0:00:00 — Tokyo Cherry Blossom Highlights\n\n0:01:05 — Kanda: Heart of Traditional Tokyo\n\n0:07:10 — First Bloom: Entering the Sakura Zones\n\n0:52:55 — Urban Oasis & Modern Architecture\n\n1:21:45 — Shirohata Inari Shrine\n\n1:28:22 — Coredo Muromachi & Nihonbashi Vibes\n\n1:29:47 — The Great Sakura Tunnel (150+ Trees)\n\n1:53:24 — Fukutoku Shrine: Ancient Sanctuary\n\n2:11:08 — The Historic Nihonbashi Bridge\n\n2:48:46 — Ginza 1-chome: Gateway to Luxury\n\n2:58:05 — Ginza Chuo-dori: Premier Avenue\n\n3:17:11 — Architectural Landmark: Ginza Lion\n\n3:29:48 — Shimbashi Transit Hub\n\n3:37:36 — Karasumori Shrine: Final Destination\n🔔 Subscribe for more Tokyo walking tour videos\n\n👍 Like if this cherry blossom season walking tour interested you\n\n#TokyoWalkingTour #CherryBlossomWalk #SakuraWalk #JapanWalkingTour #TokyoSpring #WalkingTour #JapanTravel","thumbnail":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/BbCOFlpC-MQ/maxresdefault.jpg","category":"Walking Tours","channel":"Tokyo Walking","channelTitle":"Tokyo Walking","channelId":"UCdN5xaPBQWRSbKq1kAI7fEQ","badge":"4K 60FPS","publishedAt":"2024-03-17T09:30:02Z","admission":{"version":1,"status":"accepted","uniqueEvidenceCount":14,"evidence":[{"title":"— Tokyo Cherry Blossom Highlights","startSeconds":0},{"title":"— Kanda: Heart of Traditional Tokyo","startSeconds":65},{"title":"— First Bloom: Entering the Sakura Zones","startSeconds":430},{"title":"— Urban Oasis & Modern Architecture","startSeconds":3175},{"title":"— Shirohata Inari Shrine","startSeconds":4905},{"title":"— Coredo Muromachi & Nihonbashi Vibes","startSeconds":5302},{"title":"— The Great Sakura Tunnel","startSeconds":5387},{"title":"— Fukutoku Shrine: Ancient Sanctuary","startSeconds":6804},{"title":"— The Historic Nihonbashi Bridge","startSeconds":7868},{"title":"— Ginza 1-chome: Gateway to Luxury","startSeconds":10126},{"title":"— Ginza Chuo-dori: Premier Avenue","startSeconds":10685},{"title":"— Architectural Landmark: Ginza Lion","startSeconds":11831},{"title":"— Shimbashi Transit Hub","startSeconds":12588},{"title":"— Karasumori Shrine: Final Destination","startSeconds":13056}]}}',
