VALUES (
  'aWLS-ki724M',
  'The Quiet Suburban Side of Tokyo That Feels Like Countryside Walk | Japan 4K HDR',
  'Take a peaceful Tokyo walking tour through a quiet neighborhood with a nostalgic countryside vibe during the beautiful evening twilight.
Experience a peaceful evening stroll through Tokyo’s unique neighborhood, walking from Chikatetsu-Akatsuka Station to the quiet Hikarigaoka Station area. Captured on a pleasant evening in late June, this walk showcases the gradual shift from nostalgic local shopping streets to the vast, green park surrounded by calm residential areas. Catch a glimpse of authentic local life in Tokyo along the peaceful residential pathways under the twilight, before diving into the serene greenery and hearing the gentle sound of frogs. A perfect one-hour twilight journey for those who love real Tokyo.

Filmed in 4K HDR with high quality stereo sound.
The Google Maps link below shows the full walking route with chapter timestamps.

Don’t forget to like, comment, and subscribe for more Tokyo walking tours.

[Google Maps / Chapters]
https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/edit?mid=1FvX6o2rt9j_mCrwK_ZWtuBS5Zj5o0pI&usp=sharing

0:00 Preview
1:00 [1] Start: Chikatetsu-Akatsuka Station
2:54 [2] Shimo-Akatsuka Station
21:38 [3] Yurinoki Shopping Street
37:24 [4] Aki-no-hi (Autumn Sunlight) Park
47:27 [5] Hikarigaoka Park
54:19 [6] Hikarigaoka Incineration Plant Chimney
1:04:12 [7] End: Hikarigaoka Station

[Details]
Location: Itabashi City and Nerima City, Tokyo
Time: Around 7:00 PM for about 1 hour
Season: Late June
Weather: Cloudy with sunny intervals
Temperature: 24.8°C / 76.6°F
Wind: South 1.2 m/s
Route: From Chikatetsu-Akatsuka Station to Hikarigaoka Station
Quality: 4K/60fps/HDR
Audio: 48kHz/24bit High-Quality Stereo
Subtitles: Multilingual available

