VALUES (
  '0Dd3BjjNvEA',
  'They’re Not Angry. It’s Just Manhattan Before 9AM | NYC 4K Walk',
  'Manhattan before 9AM is fast walkers, office commuters, yellow taxis and a sidewalk rush that can look tougher than it feels. This NYC 4K walking tour follows Eighth Avenue from the Theater District through the Garment District, Penn Station, Hudson Yards and Macy’s Herald Square.

Filmed on a Tuesday morning, this walk begins where the Theater District meets Hell’s Kitchen. We pass the Port Authority Bus Terminal, the New York Times Building and the historic Garment District before reaching the New Yorker Hotel, Madison Square Garden and Moynihan Train Hall.

From there, the route moves through Manhattan West and Hudson Yards—home to the Vessel, Edge and the High Line—then returns past B&H Photo, Penn Station and the Empire State Building before ending at Macy’s in Herald Square.

Fifty-three minutes of real Midtown Manhattan before 9AM: business clothes, packed sidewalks, subway-bound commuters and the rhythm of New York getting to work. All in 4K, with no narration—just authentic city sounds.

🗓️ Filmed: Aug 4, 2026 | Tuesday | 8:38 AM  | | ☀️ 78°F (25°C)
🎧 No narration | Subtitles available in 10 languages

