VALUES (
  '_Xo9XZvbtwM',
  'World''s Best Singapore Changi Airport Full Tour | Overnight in Jewel Changi Airport | Travel Vlog',
  'Today, we''ll take a thorough look at Singapore Changi Airport, famous as one of the world''s best airports.

We''ll explore each floor of the Jewel complex, see the indoor waterfall Rain Vortex, and spend the night at a hotel within Jewel. Furthermore, we''ll check out the departure halls and restricted areas  (transit areas) of each terminal.

Singapore Changi Airport
Official Name: Singapore Changi International Airport
Opening Date: July 1, 1981
Owner: Government of Singapore
Operator: Changi Airport Group

Terminal 1
Opening Date: July 1, 1981
Floor Area: 280,020 sq m
Maximum Passenger Capacity: 21 million

Terminal 2
Opening Date: January 22, 1990
Floor Area: 358,000 sq m
Maximum Passenger Capacity: 23 million

Terminal 3
Opening Date: January 9, 2008
Floor Area: 380,000 sq m
Maximum Passenger Capacity: 22 million

Terminal 4
Opening Date: October 31, 2017
Floor Area: 225,000 sq m
Maximum Passenger Capacity: 16 million

Terminal 5
Scheduled Opening Date: Mid-2030s

Jewel
Opening Date: April 17, 2019
Floor Area: 135,700 sq m

Jewel is a large-scale mixed-use complex (shopping mall and entertainment facility) connected to Terminals 1, 2, and 3. The total construction cost was approximately 1.7 billion Singapore dollars (about 1.25 billion US dollars). Designed by world-renowned architect Moshe Safdie (who also designed Marina Bay Sands), it features a massive, dome-shaped exterior made of glass and steel.

・Table of Contents
00:00 Intro
00:46 Rain Vortex, the world''s tallest indoor waterfall located inside Jewel
02:30 Jewel''s 5th Floor - Canopy Park, an interactive entertainment facility
09:01 Jewel''s 4th Floor - Various shops
10:55 Jewel''s 3rd Floor - Restaurants, etc.
13:15 Jewel''s 2nd Floor - Global brand shops, etc.
15:29 Jewel''s 1st Floor - Airport service facilities, etc.
17:11 Jewel''s Basement 1 - Apparel shops, food court, etc.
18:37 Jewel''s Basement 2 - Food court, convenience store, cinema, etc.
20:42 Departure Halls of Each Terminal (Landside)
29:10 Nighttime show at Rain Vortex, the indoor waterfall
31:55 Spending the night at a Hotel on the 4th floor of Jewel
41:50 Experience Studio - The History and Behind the Scenes of Changi Airport
48:10 Transit/Restricted Area of ​​Terminal 2 (Airside)
52:37 Transit/Restricted Area of ​​Terminal 1 (Airside)
57:16 Transit/Restricted Area of ​​Terminal 3 (Airside)
1:01:15 Thank you for watching

