VALUES (
  'DHYz7iR4Rw0',
  'Quiet Evening Walk in Tokyo’s Local Side: Old Shinagawa Alleys | Japan 4K HDR',
  'Discover the charm of a quiet evening walk in Tokyo’s local side as we explore the nostalgic retro streets of Shinagawa Ward. Filmed in early August at around 6:30 PM, this relaxing walk takes you from Fudō-mae Station to Ebara-Nakanobu Station during the peaceful twilight hour. Enjoy the authentic atmosphere of historic temples and sacred shrines, while passing through a section of the famous Togoshi Ginza Shopping Street under the cooling summer sky. A perfect journey for travelers looking to experience the hidden suburban side of real Tokyo.

Filmed in 4K HDR with high quality stereo sound.
The Google Maps link below shows the full walking route with chapter timestamps.

Don’t forget to like, comment, and subscribe for more Tokyo walking tours.

[Google Maps / Chapters]
https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/edit?mid=1Uk2sZuARyLjKIoI1NzL5ea995CuQIBM&usp=sharing

0:00 Preview
1:00 [1] Start: Fudō-mae Station
16:12 [2] Chōouji Temple
43:11 [3] Togoshi Jizoson
47:45 [4] Togoshi Ginza Shopping Street
1:02:57 [5] End: Ebara-Nakanobu Station

[Details]
Location: Shinagawa City, Tokyo
Time: Around 6:30 PM for about 1 hour
Season: Early August
Weather: Mostly sunny
Temperature: 29.3°C / 84.7°F
Wind: SSW 6.4 m/s
Route: From Fudō-mae Station to Ebara-Nakanobu Station
Quality: 4K/60fps/HDR
Audio: 48kHz/24bit High-Quality Stereo
Subtitles: Multilingual available

🥷 TokyoNinjaWalk playlists
