VALUES (
  '7CIVORlqt3Y',
  'Istanbul, Turkey in 4K – A Mesmerizing Walk Through the Historic City',
  'Step into the heart of Istanbul as the city glows under the evening sky! 🌙✨ Walk with me through history as we explore stunning landmarks, lively bazaars, and ancient streets in this immersive 4K walking tour. This evening walking tour takes you through the city''s most iconic landmarks. Wander past the breathtaking Hagia Sophia Grand Mosque, explore the charming Arasta Bazaar, and marvel at the Blue Mosque as night falls. Along the way, we''ll visit ancient monuments like the Column of Constantine, the Serpent Column, and the German Fountain, weaving through vibrant streets and hidden alleys.

📅 *Filmed on* Sunday, September 15th, 2024, starting at 6:38 PM in Sultan Ahmet Park.
🌞 *Weather*   27°C | 80°F🌡

🗺️ *Map of the Walk* https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/edit?mid=1hMyh2kTFw9q8fSjjUYFuXbpwEsQVmn0&usp=sharing  🗺️

🔻𝗩𝗶𝗱𝗲𝗼 𝗧𝗶𝗺𝗲𝗹𝗶𝗻𝗲 𝗟𝗶𝗻𝗸𝘀🔻
⏳ 0:00 Intro & Map
🌳 1:29 Sultan Ahmet Park
🕌 6:59 Hagia Sophia Grand Mosque (Ayasofya)
🛍 18:07 Arasta Bazaar
🏛 29:29 Constantine Obelisk
🐍 31:12 Serpent Column
🏛 32:13 Obelisk of Theodosius (Egyptian Obelisk)
🕌 36:02 The Blue Mosque
🏰 44:21 Sultanahmet Square
⛲ 45:56 German Fountain
🚶 53:29 Yerebatan Cd & Hidden Alleys
🏛 1:11:17 Column of Constantine
✨ 1:13:08 Nuruosmaniye Mosque & Grand Finale

🏛 *Did You Know?* The Column of Constantine, built in AD 330, marks the spot where Constantinople was officially declared the capital of the Roman Empire by Emperor Constantine the Great.

🕌 *Fun Fact:* The Hagia Sophia has transformed from a cathedral to a mosque, then a museum, and is now an active mosque again. It has stood for nearly 1,500 years!

💬 *What’s your favorite landmark in Istanbul?* Have you visited any of these places? Drop your thoughts in the comments below!

🌙 *Join me* for this immersive evening stroll through Istanbul’s historic district! Don''t forget to like, comment, and subscribe for more walking tours! 🚶‍♂️✨

