VALUES (
  'cBnw73N0yMs',
  'This Is What New Yorkers Walk Past Before 9AM | Park Avenue to Chelsea 4K',
  'Ever wondered what New Yorkers walk past every morning before 9AM?

On a clear Thursday morning in Manhattan, I started on Park Avenue and walked through Rockefeller Center, down 6th Avenue past Bryant Park, into Herald Square, past Madison Square Garden and Penn Station, through the Flower District, and finished at Ladies’ Mile in Chelsea.

This 50-minute NYC walking tour captures the morning commute in full swing — suited professionals rushing to work, yellow taxis, opening food carts, the TODAY Show broadcasting live, an NYPD briefing outside MSG, and all the small details most people walk past without stopping.

Filmed in 4K with no narration — just real New York City sounds.

🗓️ Filmed: Jun 25, 2026 | Thursday | 8:39 AM | ☀️ 72°F (22°C)
🎧 No narration | Subtitles available in 10 languages

00:00 Park Avenue before 9AM
01:43 Blackstone on Park Avenue
06:31 Rockefeller Center & Channel Gardens
09:10 TODAY Show Studio at Rockefeller Plaza
11:30 Walking down 6th Avenue
19:32 42nd Street morning rush
24:03 Broadway toward Herald Square
26:12 Morning Dunkin’ line on 34th Street
28:41 Herald Square & Macy’s
29:34 Empire State Building view
30:46 34th Street traffic & yellow cabs
32:51 7th Avenue toward Penn Station
34:25 Madison Square Garden & Penn Station
35:31 NYPD briefing outside MSG
38:50 Fashion Institute of Technology
39:26 Entering the Flower District
