  '{"id":"6bpQXDTyaeI","title":"Rome Italy 🇮🇹 Beautiful sunny day discovering the Eternal City | Bustling City Streets Walk [4K]","description":"SUBSCRIBE for more videos: https://www.youtube.com/c/KrielJan?sub_confirmation=1\nSUPPORT Kriel Jan via PayPal 🙏: https://www.paypal.com/donate/?hosted_button_id=JMWFKQFYXXTTJ\n\nRome is Italy’s capital and its most populous municipality. It also serves as the administrative center of the Lazio region and the Metropolitan City of Rome. Often called the “City of Seven Hills” because of its landscape, it is also known as the “Eternal City.” Widely regarded as a cornerstone of Western civilization and Christian culture, Rome is the heart of the Catholic Church.\n\nWith a history stretching back over 28 centuries, Rome’s origins are steeped in legend, with mythology placing its founding around 753 BC—though the area had been inhabited long before then. This makes it one of the oldest continuously occupied cities in Europe. Its early inhabitants included Latins, Etruscans, and Sabines, and over time it rose to become the capital of the Roman Kingdom, the Roman Republic, and eventually the Roman Empire. Many consider it the world’s first true imperial city and metropolis. The term “Eternal City” was first used by the poet Tibullus in the 1st century BC and later echoed by writers like Ovid, Virgil, and Livy. Rome is also known as Caput Mundi, meaning “Capital of the World.”\n\nIn 2019, Rome ranked as the 14th most visited city globally, attracting 8.6 million tourists. It was the third most visited city in the European Union and Italy’s top travel destination. Its historic center is recognized as a UNESCO World Heritage Site.\n\nToday, Rome remains one of the world’s leading tourist destinations, celebrated for its vast array of archaeological and artistic treasures. Visitors are drawn not only to its historic landmarks but also to its rich traditions, scenic views, and the grandeur of its famous villas and parks. Highlights include its renowned museums—such as the Capitoline Museums, the Vatican Museums, and the Galleria Borghese—alongside aqueducts, fountains, churches, palaces, ancient ruins like the Roman Forum, and the Catacombs.\n\n📅 26 April 2026 · Sunday\n⏰ 04:56pm (23ºC/73.4ºF)\n\nSee · Feel · Enjoy Andalucía\n\n⏳ Timestamps\n00:00 In this video\n01:30 Piazza del Popolo\n04:20 Via del Corso\n17:04 Via dei Condotti\n22:55 Piazza di Spagna\n24:48 Scalinata di Trinità dei Monti (Spanish steps)\n30:22 Piazza di Spagna\n34:32 Via di Propaganda\n37:10 Via di Sant''Andrea delle Fratte\n39:20 Largo del Nazareno\n40:54 Via Poli\n41:37 Via del Tritone\n41:59 Via Poli\n44:12 Fontana di Trevi\n47:19 Via delle Muratte\n52:41 Via di Pietra\n54:14 Piazza di Pietra\n55:55 Via dei Pastini\n59:35 Piazza della Rotonda\n59:55 Panteón\n1:01:25 Piazza della Rotonda\n1:03:35 Via dei Gustiniani\n1:06:07 Chiesa di San Luigi dei Francesi\n1:06:28 Via del Salvatore\n1:07:30 Corso del Rinascimento\n1:08:28 Corsia Agonale\n1:08:52 Piazza Navona\n1:09:25 Fontana dei Quattro Fiumi\n1:09:42 Piazza Navona\n1:14:12 Via di Pasquino\n1:14:52 Piazza di Pasquino\n1:15:55 Via del Governo Vecchio\n1:21:53 Via dei Banchi Nuovi\n1:25:30 Via del Banco di Santo Spirito\n1:28:00 Ponte Sant''Angelo\n1:31:10 Castel Sant''Angelo\n1:31:25 Lungotevere Castello\n1:34:01 Lungotevere Vaticano\n1:34:32 Piazza Pia\n1:35:16 Via della Conciliazione\n1:41:28 Piazza di San Pietro (St. Peter''s Square)\n1:45:05 Basilica di San Pietro\n1:46:03 Outro\n\nMy playlists 😃✅\nMÁLAGA CITY: https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLI3oSPGxa-48cqZO5MgGDzvE8bmxIx1BG\nTORREMOLINOS: https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLI3oSPGxa-4_-PDn6K0C8hdqT7MZNzhAu\nLA CARIHUELA: https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLI3oSPGxa-4-TcedPrG8i1XS6e9l55Qeb\nBENALMÁDENA: https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLI3oSPGxa-48nXkHZe_d49QNa_XEXqcW4\nFUENGIROLA: https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLI3oSPGxa-480FxAlNpGGZEGT_wXHn_4d\nLOS BOLICHES: https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLI3oSPGxa-4_h7GB