Ecuador (Equator in Spanish) is a country in South America. Ecuador is one of the most diverse countries in the world. The country hosts many endemic animals and plants. Also the famous Galápagos Islands are part of Ecuador which were described by Charles Darwin for its unique ecosystem. The capital of Ecuador is Quito which has the biggest colonial center of all the cities in South America. Ecuador has a population of 18 million people of which 3 million live in the metropolitan area of Quito. Ecuador was after its discovery by the Spanish in the 15th century colonized during the 16th century. Spanish is still the official language although also some native languages are recognized as Shuar and Quechua (Inca languages). Ecuador was once part of the Inca Empire before the colonization of the Spanish.

