  '{"id":"DpEWz7kfGRU","title":"LEIPZIG, Germany 🇩🇪 4K Walking Tour | Old Town, Shopping Streets & Summer City Life","description":"🖼️ Prints of my travel photos (EU/UK)*: https://juniqe.com/p/cbqwrlpm\n🌍 Prints of my travel photos (worldwide)*: https://www.goodmoodprints.com/artists/boldandretro?artist=HXSBQue3HfM9M11Y5UgV\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nWhat does Leipzig feel like on a hot summer Saturday? Join this full-length 4K walking tour through the heart of Leipzig, Germany, filmed in bright sunshine at around 29°C / 84°F. 🇩🇪☀️\n\nThe 1 hour 43 minute walk begins at Augustusplatz and explores Leipzig’s lively city center at street level. We follow busy shopping streets, enter historic arcades and modern malls, pass packed restaurant terraces and discover landmarks including Leipzig Opera, the City-Hochhaus, Specks Hof, the Old Stock Exchange, Mädler Passage, Market Square, the Old Town Hall and St. Thomas Church.\n\nThe route continues through Petersstraße, Messehof Passage, Reichsstraße and Höfe am Brühl before ending at Willy-Brandt-Platz with a view of Leipzig Central Station. This is not an empty-city walk: it captures the authentic atmosphere of a popular German city on a sunny August weekend.\n\nWatch it as virtual travel, use it to plan a Leipzig city trip or enjoy more than 100 minutes of real urban ambience on a big TV, computer or phone.\n\n🎧 No narration and no added music – only authentic street sounds, conversations, shops, restaurants and city ambience recorded during the walk.\n\n💬 Which part of Leipzig would you explore first: the historic passages, St. Thomas Church or the busy shopping streets?\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n📍 WALK INFORMATION\n\n📍 Location: Leipzig, Saxony, Germany\n🚶 Route: Augustusplatz → Old Town → shopping streets and passages → Central Station\n☀️ Weather: Sunny Saturday in August, around 29°C / 84°F\n🎧 Audio: Real ambient sounds, no narration or added music\n⏱️ Duration: 1 hour 43 minutes\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🗺️ CHAPTERS\n\n00:00 Start of the walk at Augustusplatz\n00:10 Mendebrunnen fountain\n02:51 Leipzig Opera and public drinking fountain\n03:55 City-Hochhaus\n05:35 Democracy Bell\n06:10 Faculty of Mathematics and Computer Science\n06:30 Grimmaische Straße\n06:50 “Unzeitgemäße Zeitgenossen” sculpture\n09:18 Brief look into Nikolaistraße\n10:15 Specks Hof and Hansa Haus\n10:40 Small fountain in Specks Hof\n14:10 Naschmarkt\n14:15 Lion Fountain\n15:15 Old Stock Exchange\n16:00 Goethe Monument\n17:20 “The Step of the Century” by Wolfgang Mattheuer\n19:50 Mädler Passage\n23:25 Leipzig Market Square\n23:45 Archway through the Old Town Hall\n24:45 Memorial plaque for the Leipzig witch persecutions\n25:40 Salzgässchen\n26:30 Old Town Hall\n27:05 Katharinenstraße\n28:50 Art-filled green courtyard\n31:22 Museum of Fine Arts Leipzig\n34:30 Brühl\n36:40 Hainstraße\n41:00 Barthels Hof\n43:00 Stage for the Leipziger Markt Musik event\n44:45 Barfußgässchen\n46:45 Lipsia Fountain\n48:00 Klostergasse\n49:15 Marktgalerie\n51:40 St. Thomas Church\n55:40 Dittrichring\n56:50 Old Bach Monument near St. Thomas Church\n58:30 Plato Dolz Monument by Hermann Knaur\n01:00:00 Thomaskirchhof\n01:01:55 New Bach Monument in front of St. Thomas Church\n01:03:20 Burgstraße\n01:06:25 New Town Hall tower\n01:06:45 Petersbogen shopping center\n01:07:50 Schloßgasse\n01:09:30 Wilhelm-Leuschner-Platz\n01:10:00 Petersstraße\n01:10:50 Peterskirchhof\n01:15:50 Thomaswiese\n01:20:00 Messehof Passage\n01:23:50 Street performer with a handmade drum kit\n01:26:20 Reichsstraße\n01:29:35 Riquet House\n01:30:40 “Young Couple” sculpture by Klaus Schwabe\n01:34:30 Höfe am Brühl shopping center\n01:38:00 Richard-Wagner-Straße\n01:40:00 Am Hallischen Tor\n01:42:45 Willy-Brandt-Platz and Leipzig Central Station\n01:43:20 End of the Leipzig walk\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n📍 ABOUT LEIPZIG CITY CENTER\n\nLeipzig’s compact center combines historic trade courtyards, elegant passages, shopping streets, restaurants and major music landmarks. The 140-meter Mädler Passage was built from 1912 to 1914. Johann Sebastian Bach worked at St. Thomas Church from 1723 to 1750, while Leipzig Central Station forms a monumental gateway to the city center.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎥 MORE FROM LEIPZIG\n\nLeipzig Christmas Market in 4K\nhttps://youtu.be/2TG93BauDVE\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n☕ SUPPORT MARTIN WALKS\n\nhttps://buymeacoffee.com/martinwalks\n\n📸 Instagram\nhttps://instagram.com/martinwalkstv\n\n*Affiliate link / Ad: I may earn a small commission from qualifying purchases at no extra cost to you. Thank you for supporting the channel!\n\n#Leipzig #LeipzigGermany #LeipzigWalkingTour #GermanyWalkingTour #MartinWalks","thumbnail":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/DpEWz7kfGRU/maxresdefault.jpg","category":"Museums & Culture","channel":"Martin Walks 🌍 Walking Tours","channelTitle":"Martin Walks 🌍 Walking Tours","channelId":"UCP99mHsQzWTt5_z3XTo61sQ","badge":"4K 60FPS","publishedAt":"2026-08-16T05:30:15Z","admission":{"version":1,"status":"accepted","uniqueEvidenceCount":30,"evidence":[{"title":"Start of the walk at Augustusplatz","startSeconds":0},{"title":"Mendebrunnen fountain","startSeconds":10},{"title":"Leipzig Opera and public drinking fountain","startSeconds":171},{"title":"City-Hochhaus","startSeconds":235},{"title":"Democracy Bell","startSeconds":335},{"title":"Faculty of Mathematics and Computer Science","startSeconds":370},{"title":"Grimmaische Straße","startSeconds":390},{"title":"“Unzeitgemäße Zeitgenossen” sculpture","startSeconds":410},{"title":"Brief look into Nikolaistraße","startSeconds":558},{"title":"Specks Hof and Hansa Haus","startSeconds":615},{"title":"Small fountain in Specks Hof","startSeconds":640},{"title":"Naschmarkt","startSeconds":850},{"title":"Lion Fountain","startSeconds":855},{"title":"Old Stock Exchange","startSeconds":915},{"title":"Goethe Monument","startSeconds":960},{"title":"“The Step of the Century” by Wolfgang Mattheuer","startSeconds":1040},{"title":"Mädler Passage","startSeconds":1190},{"title":"Leipzig Mar